IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lt-common`

-- Land Tax Act 2000 (Tas), read with the Land Tax Rating Act 2000 (Tas) and the Land Tax Regulations 2021 (Tas) --
-- the seat-neutral core.
--
-- Rules in the Acts' own actors and terms: the owner (s 3A), the taxpayer, the related person, the Commissioner of
-- State Revenue. Where the text says "must" or sets a deadline, the rule is regulative (DEONTIC). Computations are
-- functions. The owner's questions are asked in lta-seat.l4, which restates none of these rules.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: ss 3 (definitions used), 3A(1)-(2), 3B; s 6(1), (2), (8), (9)-(12); ss 7, 8; s 10(1)-(2) with
-- s 39(10) (the relevant day); s 11(3); s 11(5)-(6) (regulative); s 11A; s 13; s 14(1)-(2); s 16 (regulative);
-- s 19(a)-(b) with Land Tax Regulations 2021 reg 5; ss 20, 23 (the value an input), 24(1)-(1A); s 26 with s 3
-- "qualifying home business"; s 27; s 37 (regulative); s 37A (regulative); s 37B. Land Tax Rating Act 2000 ss 4, 5, 6,
-- 7 and Schedule 1.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: foreign investor land tax (Div 1A; Rating Act s 6A); trusts, companies and home-unit companies
-- (s 6(3)-(5), ss 24(2)-(4), 28, 31-35, Div 5); cooperative housing societies (s 30); retirement village land and the
-- other exemptions (ss 17, 18, 19(ba)-(e), 19A-19EA, 29, 30A); subdivisions (ss 23(2), 25); the special rate (s 38);
-- recovery (ss 39-40, except the s 39(10) "relevant day" that s 10(2) borrows); s 12 (assessment and reassessment);
-- s 11(1), (4) (the Commissioner's list of owners and the Valuer-General's details: machinery); s 36 (onus) except as
-- a note; reg 4 (owners of land not under the Land Titles Act 1980); the Taxation Administration Act 1997. Where
-- foreign investor land tax or one of the other exemptions may reach the land, the amount answers `not covered`
-- (finding 24).
--
-- Edition: Land Tax Act 2000 consolidation published 2026-10-14 (../../registers/source-bundle/act-2000-074.txt);
-- Land Tax Rating Act 2000 consolidation published 2024-07-12; Land Tax Regulations 2021 version published
-- 2021-12-01; all current on the Tasmanian Legislation website at 2026-10-20. Copyright State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0.
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 20 October 2026. For the latest information on
-- Tasmanian Government legislation please go to www.legislation.tas.gov.au.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land Tax Act 2000 and Land Tax Rating Act 2000 -- the core`

§§ `The years covered`

-- The deposited consolidation shows ss 13 and 37 as amended by No. 19 of 2026 (applied 1 July 2026) and not their
-- earlier wording. Schedule 1 to the Rating Act was last amended from 1 July 2024 (No. 5 of 2024). So 2026-27 is the
-- first financial year for which every provision encoded here is the one deposited.
`the first financial year covered by the land tax provisions` MEANS 2026

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposited land tax provisions apply to` IF
    `the financial year` AT LEAST `the first financial year covered by the land tax provisions`

§§ `ss 3A, 3B and 11A -- the owner and the owner's interest`

-- s 3A(1): "owner means -- (a) the person in whom the estate in fee simple is vested". (1A): that person is, unless
-- the Commissioner on reasonable grounds determines otherwise, the person who appears from a folio of the Register
-- to be the owner. (2): "If a person appears by a folio of the Register ... to be entitled ... to an estate of freehold
-- for his or her life, that person is taken to be the owner of the land instead of the person entitled to the estate
-- in fee simple in remainder." (Owners of land not under the Land Titles Act 1980, reg 4, are not encoded.)
DECLARE `Title` IS ONE OF
    `registered owner of the fee simple, with no life estate in another person`
    `registered as entitled to a life estate`
    `owner of the fee simple in remainder after another person's life estate`
    `no estate in the land`

GIVEN `the title` IS A `Title`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an owner under s 3A` IF
    CONSIDER `the title`
    WHEN `registered owner of the fee simple, with no life estate in another person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `registered as entitled to a life estate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The interest one owner holds. s 3B: "joint tenants in relation to land are to be taken to be tenants in common in
-- equal shares in relation to the land." s 11A(2): for land purchased under a Help to Buy arrangement (Help to Buy Act
-- 2024 of the Commonwealth), "including the application of any exemptions or concessions ..., no account is to be
-- taken of any interest that the Commonwealth or Housing Australia has in the land as a result of the arrangement".
-- READING (finding 4): leaving that interest out of account makes the other owners' interests the whole, so each
-- interest is measured against the land less the Help to Buy share.
DECLARE `Holding` HAS
    `share of the land held, in percent` IS A NUMBER
    `number of joint tenants of that share` IS A NUMBER
    `Help to Buy share of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia, in percent` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the holding` IS A `Holding`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest in percent counted for land tax` MEANS
    (`the holding`'s `share of the land held, in percent` DIVIDED BY `the holding`'s `number of joint tenants of that share`)
        TIMES 100
        DIVIDED BY (100 MINUS `the holding`'s `Help to Buy share of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia, in percent`)

-- s 6(1), s 6(2)(d), s 19(a)-(b), s 37(1)(b), s 37A(4): "an owner of at least a 50% interest", "owned 50% or more".
GIVEN `the holding` IS A `Holding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an owner of at least a 50% interest` IF
    `the interest in percent counted for land tax` `the holding` AT LEAST 50

§§ `s 6 -- principal residence land`

-- s 3: "principal residence means a dwelling used as the main place of residence". "related person, in relation to an
-- owner, means -- (a) the spouse or former spouse of the owner; or (b) if the owner is deceased, the beneficiary of
-- the estate of the owner; or (c) a beneficiary of a trust appointed by a court; or (d) a shareholder of a home-unit
-- company or a spouse or former spouse of the shareholder; or (e) a person with an exclusive right to occupy a flat
-- owned by a retirement village or a spouse or former spouse of that person; or (f) the person with whom the owner is
-- in a caring relationship" registered under Part 2 of the Relationships Act 2003. "spouse" includes a person in a
-- significant relationship (Relationships Act 2003). These are facts.
--
-- s 6(1): "Principal residence land is land on which the principal residence of an owner of at least a 50% interest in
-- the land or a related person of such an owner is situated."
-- s 6(8): "If a person occupies residential premises in a retirement village as his or her principal place of
-- residence, any other land owned by the person is not that person's principal place of residence."
-- s 37B(2): during a s 37B extension, "the owner of the principal residence land is not entitled to have any other land
-- classified as principal residence land".
-- The Act sets no date in s 6(1); s 20(1)(a) values the land "as at 1 July", s 6(3)(b) and (4)(b) and s 6(10) speak of
-- 1 July, and s 10(1) fixes liability at the commencement of the financial year. The facts are as at 1 July.
DECLARE `Residence at 1 July` HAS
    `the principal residence of an owner of at least a 50% interest is on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that owner occupies premises in a retirement village as their principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the principal residence of a related person of such an owner is on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a s 37B extension is in force for other land of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the residence` IS A `Residence at 1 July`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is principal residence land under s 6(1)` IF
        (    (    `the residence`'s `the principal residence of an owner of at least a 50% interest is on the land`
              AND (NOT (`the residence`'s `that owner occupies premises in a retirement village as their principal place of residence`)))
         OR  `the residence`'s `the principal residence of a related person of such an owner is on the land`)
    AND (NOT (`the residence`'s `a s 37B extension is in force for other land of the owner`))

-- s 6(2): "The Commissioner is to determine that adjoining land is principal residence land if satisfied that -- (a)
-- the land is on a separate title held by the owner of the principal residence land; and (ab) there is no dwelling on
-- the land that is used as a place of residence; and (b) the land is used by that owner solely in conjunction with the
-- principal residence land; and (c) the owner does not receive any income from the use of that land; and (d) the owner
-- of at least a 50% interest in the principal residence land is also the owner of at least a 50% interest in the
-- adjoining land." TRUE means: yes, if the Commissioner is satisfied of these facts.
DECLARE `Adjoining land` HAS
    `adjoins the principal residence land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is on a separate title held by the owner of the principal residence land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has no dwelling used as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is used by that owner solely in conjunction with the principal residence land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner receives no income from its use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner of at least 50% of the principal residence land owns at least 50% of this land` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the land` IS AN `Adjoining land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is principal residence land under s 6(2)` IF
        `the land`'s `adjoins the principal residence land`
    AND `the land`'s `is on a separate title held by the owner of the principal residence land`
    AND `the land`'s `has no dwelling used as a place of residence`
    AND `the land`'s `is used by that owner solely in conjunction with the principal residence land`
    AND `the land`'s `the owner receives no income from its use`
    AND `the land`'s `the owner of at least 50% of the principal residence land owns at least 50% of this land`

-- s 6(9): subsections (10) and (11) apply only if, but for them, the land would not be principal residence land.
-- s 6(10): they apply to land for a financial year beginning on 1 July (the assessment day) if "(a) at 1 July in the
-- previous financial year (... the critical date), land is principal residence land under subsection (1); and (b) the
-- person who -- (i) was the sole owner of the land on the critical date; or (ii) is a person who the Commissioner
-- determines is to be taken to be the sole owner ... -- dies on or after the critical date and before the assessment
-- day; and (c) the principal residence of that person was, on the critical date, situated on the land; and (d) the land
-- is not, after the critical date and before the assessment day -- (i) sold in whole or in part; or (ii) transferred,
-- in whole or in part, other than to the personal representative of the deceased person."
-- s 6(11): then "(a) the land is taken to be, on the assessment day, principal residence land; and (b) section 26 does
-- not apply in relation to the land for the relevant financial year."
DECLARE `After a sole owner's death` HAS
    `the land was principal residence land under s 6(1) on the previous 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sole owner on that day died on or after it and before this 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that owner's principal residence was on the land on the previous 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land has not since been sold or transferred, other than to the personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the land` IS AN `After a sole owner's death`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `continues as principal residence land under s 6(10)-(11)` IF
        `the land`'s `the land was principal residence land under s 6(1) on the previous 1 July`
    AND `the land`'s `the sole owner on that day died on or after it and before this 1 July`
    AND `the land`'s `that owner's principal residence was on the land on the previous 1 July`
    AND `the land`'s `the land has not since been sold or transferred, other than to the personal representative`

-- s 6(12): adjoining land continues too if "(b) another area of land was, at the critical date, adjoining land under
-- subsection (2) ...; and (c) the adjoining land satisfies, on the assessment day, the requirements of subsection
-- (2)(a), (ab) and (d); and (d) no income is derived from the adjoining land after the critical date and before the
-- assessment day; and (e) the adjoining land is not ... sold ... or transferred ... other than to the personal
-- representative". Then it is principal residence land and s 26 does not apply to it.
DECLARE `Adjoining land after a sole owner's death` HAS
    `was adjoining principal residence land under s 6(2) on the previous 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on this 1 July is on a separate title held by the owner, with no dwelling used as a residence, and owned at least 50% by the owner of at least 50% of the main land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no income has been derived from it since the previous 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has not since been sold or transferred, other than to the personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the main land` IS AN `After a sole owner's death`, `the adjoining land` IS AN `Adjoining land after a sole owner's death`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `continues as principal residence land under s 6(12)` IF
        `continues as principal residence land under s 6(10)-(11)` `the main land`
    AND `the adjoining land`'s `was adjoining principal residence land under s 6(2) on the previous 1 July`
    AND `the adjoining land`'s `on this 1 July is on a separate title held by the owner, with no dwelling used as a residence, and owned at least 50% by the owner of at least 50% of the main land`
    AND `the adjoining land`'s `no income has been derived from it since the previous 1 July`
    AND `the adjoining land`'s `it has not since been sold or transferred, other than to the personal representative`

§§ `s 37B -- after a flood, fire or other similar disaster`

-- s 37B(1): where principal residence land "is affected by flood, fire or other similar disaster so that the land is
-- not suitable to be occupied as principal residence land, the owner ... may apply to the Commissioner ... to extend
-- the classification of that land as principal residence land for a period of up to 2 years". (3): the same for
-- primary production land. (4): no extension "unless satisfied that the flood, fire or other similar disaster was
-- outside the control of the owner of the land". (2): no other land may be principal residence land meanwhile.
`the longest s 37B extension, in years` MEANS 2

DECLARE `Disaster` HAS
    `the land is classified as principal residence land or primary production land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a flood, fire or other similar disaster made it unsuitable for that use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disaster was outside the owner's control` IS A BOOLEAN

-- TRUE means: the classification may be extended for up to 2 years, if the Commissioner is satisfied of these facts.
GIVEN `the disaster` IS A `Disaster`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the classification may be extended under s 37B` IF
        `the disaster`'s `the land is classified as principal residence land or primary production land`
    AND `the disaster`'s `a flood, fire or other similar disaster made it unsuitable for that use`
    AND `the disaster`'s `the disaster was outside the owner's control`

§§ `ss 7 and 8 -- primary production land and general land`

-- s 7(1): "Land is primary production land if it is -- (a) used substantially for the business of primary production;
-- or (b) declared a private timber reserve ...; or (c) permanent timber production zone land ...; or (d) land in
-- respect of which there is in effect a certified forest practices plan ...". s 7(2): "The business of primary
-- production means any one or more of the following carried out in a business-like manner with a reasonable
-- expectation of profit: (a) cultivating land to sell the produce ...; (b) maintaining animals or poultry for sale or
-- selling their natural increase or bodily produce; (c) keeping bees to sell their honey; (d) commercial fishing and
-- cultivating aquatic plants or animals ...; (e) cultivating or propagating for sale plants, seedlings, mushrooms or
-- orchids."
DECLARE `Primary production` HAS
    `an activity listed in s 7(2) is carried on on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is carried on in a business-like manner with a reasonable expectation of profit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land is used substantially for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land is a private timber reserve, permanent timber production zone land or under a certified forest practices plan` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the land` IS A `Primary production`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is primary production land under s 7` IF
        (    `the land`'s `an activity listed in s 7(2) is carried on on the land`
         AND `the land`'s `it is carried on in a business-like manner with a reasonable expectation of profit`
         AND `the land`'s `the land is used substantially for it`)
    OR  `the land`'s `the land is a private timber reserve, permanent timber production zone land or under a certified forest practices plan`

-- s 24(1A): "there are 3 classes of land: principal residence land, primary production land and general land".
-- s 8: "General land is land that is not -- (a) principal residence land; or (b) primary production land."
-- READING (finding 9): the Act does not say which class land takes when it is both principal residence land and
-- primary production land; it is reported as principal residence land. Both are rated at nil.
DECLARE `Land class` IS ONE OF
    `principal residence land`
    `primary production land`
    `general land`

GIVEN `principal residence` IS A BOOLEAN, `primary production` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Land class`
`the class of land that is` MEANS
    IF `principal residence`
    THEN `principal residence land`
    ELSE IF `primary production`
         THEN `primary production land`
         ELSE `general land`

§§ `s 19(a)-(b) and reg 5 -- the pensioner exemption`

-- s 19: "Land tax is not payable in respect of the following: (a) principal residence land or primary production land
-- owned 50% or more by a person in receipt of -- (i) a current Pensioner Concession Card issued under a relevant Act of
-- the Commonwealth; or (ii) a card that is prescribed to be equivalent to the card referred to in subparagraph (i); (b)
-- principal residence land or primary production land, 50% or more of which is owned by a person who is -- (i) in
-- receipt of a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 of the Commonwealth; and (ii) totally and
-- permanently incapacitated".
-- Land Tax Regulations 2021 reg 5: "a Repatriation Health Card -- For All Conditions, with a war widow or war widower
-- endorsement, issued under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 of the Commonwealth is prescribed to be equivalent to a
-- Pensioner Concession Card."
-- s 19 names no date; read with s 10(1) as at 1 July (finding 8).
DECLARE `Pensioner owner` HAS
    `owns 50% or more of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a current Pensioner Concession Card` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a Repatriation Health Card -- For All Conditions with a war widow or war widower endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `receives a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is totally and permanently incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Land class`, `the person` IS A `Pensioner owner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is exempt land under s 19(a) or (b)` IF
        (    `the class` EQUALS `principal residence land`
         OR  `the class` EQUALS `primary production land`)
    AND `the person`'s `owns 50% or more of the land`
    AND (    `the person`'s `holds a current Pensioner Concession Card`
         OR  `the person`'s `holds a Repatriation Health Card -- For All Conditions with a war widow or war widower endorsement`
         OR  (    `the person`'s `receives a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986`
              AND `the person`'s `is totally and permanently incapacitated`))

-- READING (finding 1). For the whole parcel: s 26(1) apportions "the land value of the land" when "principal residence
-- land is used for other purposes", so the land itself stays principal residence land (s 6(1)); s 19(a)-(b) say land
-- tax "is not payable in respect of" such land, and s 10(1) charges only land "that is not exempt land"; where the Act
-- confines an exemption to part of a parcel it says so, apportioning "between exempt land and general land" (ss 19A(2),
-- 19B(2), 19C(2), 29, 30A), and s 19 has no such words; and s 16A(2)(a) has to deem the apportioned part "general land"
-- for Division 1A. Read so, a pensioner's exempt parcel bears no land tax at all, including on the part of its value
-- apportioned to general land.
-- For the contrary reading: s 26(1) apportions the value "between principal residence land and general land", naming
-- the apportioned part general land; Rating Act s 6(2) says the land tax on "the apportioned assessed land value in
-- respect of any general land is to be calculated in accordance with Schedule 1", with no carve-out; and s 16A(2)(a)
-- treats that part as general land, if only for Division 1A. Read so, s 19 reaches only the principal residence part,
-- which Rating Act s 4 already rates at nil, and changes no amount.
-- This constant takes the first reading; FALSE takes the contrary one. Both are asserted in the cases.
`READING: s 19 exempts the whole parcel, including any part apportioned to general land` MEANS TRUE

§§ `ss 3 and 26 -- apportionment of principal residence land`

-- s 3: "qualifying home business means a business -- (a) operated from land on which a prescribed dwelling is located;
-- and (b) operated from that prescribed dwelling or a building ordinarily found on residential land that is not of a
-- solely commercial character; and (c) operated by a person who is the owner of the land or spouse, sibling, child or
-- parent of the owner of the land; and (d) for which the land is the sole permanent business premises of that person;
-- and (e) for the operation of which no more than 50% of the floor area of the prescribed dwelling is ordinarily used".
-- "prescribed dwelling means a permanent building of predominantly residential character affixed to land" not under a
-- closure order (a fact).
DECLARE `Home business` HAS
    `is operated from land on which a prescribed dwelling is located` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is operated from that dwelling or a building ordinarily found on residential land that is not solely commercial` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is operated by the owner, or the owner's spouse, sibling, child or parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land is that person's sole permanent business premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage of the dwelling's floor area ordinarily used for it` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the business` IS A `Home business`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a qualifying home business` IF
        `the business`'s `is operated from land on which a prescribed dwelling is located`
    AND `the business`'s `is operated from that dwelling or a building ordinarily found on residential land that is not solely commercial`
    AND `the business`'s `is operated by the owner, or the owner's spouse, sibling, child or parent`
    AND `the business`'s `the land is that person's sole permanent business premises`
    AND `the business`'s `percentage of the dwelling's floor area ordinarily used for it` AT MOST 50

-- s 26(1): "If principal residence land is used for other purposes, not including a qualifying home business, in
-- addition to the principal residence of an owner or a related person of the owner, the Commissioner is to apportion
-- the land value of the land between principal residence land and general land." (2): the principal residence part "is
-- determined by multiplying the assessed land value by the proportion of land area so used". (2A): "the land area is
-- the area of the land together with the areas of all additional floors above or below ground level (but not including
-- the ground floor) of all structures on the land". s 6(11)(b), (12): s 26 does not apply in the year after a sole
-- owner's death.
DECLARE `Land area` HAS
    `area of the land` IS A NUMBER
    `area of all additional floors above or below ground level, not the ground floor, of all structures` IS A NUMBER
    `part of that land area used for purposes other than the principal residence` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the area` IS A `Land area`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the land area under s 26(2A)` MEANS
    `the area`'s `area of the land` PLUS `the area`'s `area of all additional floors above or below ground level, not the ground floor, of all structures`

GIVEN `the area` IS A `Land area`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the proportion of land area used as the principal residence` MEANS
    (`the land area under s 26(2A)` `the area` MINUS `the area`'s `part of that land area used for purposes other than the principal residence`)
        DIVIDED BY `the land area under s 26(2A)` `the area`

GIVEN `the area` IS A `Land area`, `the other use is a qualifying home business` IS A BOOLEAN, `s 26 is disapplied by s 6(11) or (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land value is apportioned under s 26` IF
        `the area`'s `part of that land area used for purposes other than the principal residence` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (NOT `the other use is a qualifying home business`)
    AND (NOT `s 26 is disapplied by s 6(11) or (12)`)

-- The proportion of the parcel's value that stays principal residence land: the s 26(2) proportion if apportioned,
-- otherwise the whole.
GIVEN `the area` IS A `Land area`, `the other use is a qualifying home business` IS A BOOLEAN, `s 26 is disapplied by s 6(11) or (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the principal residence proportion under s 26` MEANS
    IF `the land value is apportioned under s 26` `the area` `the other use is a qualifying home business` `s 26 is disapplied by s 6(11) or (12)`
    THEN `the proportion of land area used as the principal residence` `the area`
    ELSE 1

§§ `ss 20, 23, 24 and the Land Tax Rating Act 2000 -- the amount`

-- One parcel as at 1 July. s 23(1): "The assessed land value of land is the land value as determined under the
-- Valuation of Land Act 2001 on applying any relevant adjustment factor" -- an input from the Valuer-General.
-- `proportion of the value apportioned to its class`: for principal residence land the s 26(2) proportion, for primary
-- production land the s 27(2) proportion ("the proportion of the land so used"); 1 where there is no apportionment.
-- It is not read for general land.
DECLARE `Parcel` HAS
    `assessed land value` IS A NUMBER
    `class` IS A `Land class`
    `proportion of the value apportioned to its class` IS A NUMBER
    `is exempt land` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Rating Act s 4(1)-(2) and s 5(1)-(2): the land tax on principal residence land and primary production land, and on
-- the apportioned value of either, "is nil". s 26(3) and s 27(3): "The apportioned assessed land value in respect of
-- general land is the assessed land value less the apportioned assessed land value in respect of" the other class.
-- The value is worked out on either reading of s 19 (finding 1); the encoding's answers use the READING constant.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A `Parcel`, `s 19 exempts the whole parcel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the parcel that is general land, on the reading` MEANS
    IF     `the parcel`'s `is exempt land`
       AND (    `s 19 exempts the whole parcel`
            OR  `the parcel`'s `class` EQUALS `general land`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the parcel`'s `class` EQUALS `general land`
         THEN `the parcel`'s `assessed land value`
         ELSE `the parcel`'s `assessed land value` MINUS (`the parcel`'s `assessed land value` TIMES `the parcel`'s `proportion of the value apportioned to its class`)

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A `Parcel`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the parcel that is general land` MEANS
    `the value of the parcel that is general land, on the reading` `the parcel` `READING: s 19 exempts the whole parcel, including any part apportioned to general land`

-- s 24(1): "In the case of an owner of more than one parcel of land of the same class, land tax is to be levied on the
-- aggregate assessed land value of those parcels of land as if they were a single parcel of land." READING (finding 7):
-- the general land part of an apportioned parcel is aggregated with the owner's other general land.
GIVEN `the parcels` IS A LIST OF `Parcel`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the aggregate assessed land value of general land` MEANS
    `the total of` (map `the value of the parcel that is general land` `the parcels`)

-- Rating Act s 6 and Schedule 1 (as substituted from 1 July 2021 and amended from 1 July 2024):
-- | 1. | Less than $125 000 | Nil |
-- | 2. | $125 000 - $499 999.99 | $50 and 0.45 cents for each dollar ... in excess of $125 000 |
-- | 3. | $500 000 or more | $1 737.50 and 1.5 cents for each dollar ... in excess of $500 000 |
GIVEN `value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`land tax under Schedule 1 on` MEANS
    IF `value` LESS THAN 125000
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `value` LESS THAN 500000
         THEN 50 PLUS ((`value` MINUS 125000) TIMES 0.45 DIVIDED BY 100)
         ELSE 1737.50 PLUS ((`value` MINUS 500000) TIMES 1.5 DIVIDED BY 100)

-- Rating Act s 7: "If the amount of land tax payable when converted to cents is not exactly divisible by 10, that
-- amount of land tax is to be -- (a) rounded up to the nearest amount exactly divisible by 10, if the number of cents
-- remaining is more than 5; or (b) rounded down to the nearest amount exactly divisible by 10, if the number of cents
-- remaining is 5 or less." READING (finding 6): "the number of cents remaining" keeps any fraction of a cent.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded under s 7` MEANS
    IF `the cents remaining` EQUALS 0
    THEN `amount`
    ELSE IF `the cents remaining` GREATER THAN 5
         THEN (`the cents` MINUS `the cents remaining` PLUS 10) DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE (`the cents` MINUS `the cents remaining`) DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `the cents` MEANS `amount` TIMES 100
        `the cents remaining` MEANS `the cents` MINUS (FLOOR (`the cents` DIVIDED BY 10) TIMES 10)

-- s 20(1): the amount is determined on the assessed or apportioned assessed land value as at 1 July and set at the
-- rate in the land tax rating Act. s 10(1): payable only in respect of land that is not exempt land. One case is one
-- taxpayer's land for one financial year (joint owners are one taxpayer, s 14(2)(a)).
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER, `the parcels` IS A LIST OF `Parcel`
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
`the land tax payable for the financial year on` MEANS
    IF `the deposited land tax provisions apply to` `the financial year`
    THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` (`rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` (`the aggregate assessed land value of general land` `the parcels`)))
    ELSE `not covered` `the financial year begins before 1 July 2026: sections 13 and 37 of the Land Tax Act were amended from that day (No. 19 of 2026) and the earlier wording is not in the deposited consolidation`

§§ `The edge of the encoded amount -- foreign investor land tax and the other exemptions`

-- Two parts of the Act can change the amount for an individual owner and are not encoded (finding 24).
--
-- Division 1A. s 16C(1): "an owner of land is liable to pay foreign investor land tax in respect of the land for a
-- financial year if, at the commencement of the financial year -- (a) the land is general land" capable of being
-- lawfully used solely or primarily for residential purposes (or vacant or being built on for that use) "and (b) one
-- or more owners of the land are foreign persons -- (i) who acquired an interest in the land, as a result of a
-- dutiable transaction under the Duties Act 2001, or by right of survivorship, on or after 1 July 2022; or (ii) who
-- became foreign persons, other than foreign natural persons, on or after 1 July 2022." s 16C(2): a further interest
-- acquired on or after that day draws in the whole. s 16A(2)(a): general land "includes" a part of land apportioned as
-- general land under Division 4. Rating Act s 6A(2)-(3): the tax is "2% of the assessed land value of the land", "in
-- addition to any other amount of land tax". "Foreign person" and "foreign natural person" have their Duties Act 2001
-- meanings (s 16A(1)); they are facts here. Paragraph (b) is asked; paragraph (a) and the s 16D carve-outs are not
-- worked out, so where (b) holds and the owner has any general land the amount is not covered. With no general land,
-- s 16C cannot apply, and the Schedule 1 amount stands.
--
-- The other exemptions. Land tax "is not payable" on land used for or ancillary to a retirement village (s 19(ba),
-- (bb)), on Aboriginal land (s 19(c)) or s 19(e) land, on land under a conservation covenant, wholly or by
-- apportionment (s 19A), on approved new rental properties and former short-stay properties (ss 19D, 19E), and on the
-- parts apportioned under ss 19B, 19C, 29 and 30A. Where any of them reaches the land, the amount is not covered.
DECLARE `The edge of the encoded amount` HAS
    `one or more owners are foreign persons who acquired an interest in the land by a dutiable transaction or by survivorship on or after 1 July 2022, or became foreign persons other than foreign natural persons on or after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `some of the land is exempt, wholly or partly, under Division 2 of Part 2 on a ground other than s 19(a)-(b)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the parcels`        IS A LIST OF `Parcel`
      `the edge`           IS A `The edge of the encoded amount`
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
`the land tax payable, within the encoded scope, for the financial year on` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the deposited land tax provisions apply to` `the financial year`)
    THEN `the land tax payable for the financial year on` `the financial year` `the parcels`
    ELSE IF `the edge`'s `some of the land is exempt, wholly or partly, under Division 2 of Part 2 on a ground other than s 19(a)-(b)`
         THEN `not covered` `some of the land is exempt, wholly or partly, on a ground other than s 19(a)-(b) (ss 19(ba)-(e), 19A-19E, 29, 30A), and those exemptions are not encoded`
         ELSE IF     `the edge`'s `one or more owners are foreign persons who acquired an interest in the land by a dutiable transaction or by survivorship on or after 1 July 2022, or became foreign persons other than foreign natural persons on or after that day`
                 AND `the aggregate assessed land value of general land` `the parcels` GREATER THAN 0
              THEN `not covered` `an owner of this general land may be a foreign person liable to foreign investor land tax (Land Tax Act Division 1A; Land Tax Rating Act s 6A: 2% of the assessed land value, on top of the Schedule 1 amount), which is not encoded`
              ELSE `the land tax payable for the financial year on` `the financial year` `the parcels`

§§ `ss 10, 11(3) and 14 -- who is liable, and when the tax is due`

-- s 10(1): "Land tax is payable in respect of land that is not exempt land by the person who is the owner of the land
-- as at the commencement of the financial year." s 11(3): "If there is a change in ownership of land, that change takes
-- effect on the date on which the contract for the sale of the land is completed." READING (finding 10): a sale
-- completed on 1 July takes effect after the commencement of that day, so the seller is the owner at the commencement.
DECLARE `Ownership` HAS
    `the title` IS A `Title`
    `the day the purchase was completed` IS A DATE
    `the land has been sold` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the sale was completed` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the ownership` IS AN `Ownership`, `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `was the owner at the commencement of the financial year` IF
        `is an owner under s 3A` (`the ownership`'s `the title`)
    AND `is before` (`the ownership`'s `the day the purchase was completed`) (`1 July of` `the financial year`)
    AND (    (NOT (`the ownership`'s `the land has been sold`))
         OR  `is on or before` (`1 July of` `the financial year`) (`the ownership`'s `the day the sale was completed`))

-- s 14: "(1) Land tax is payable by joint owners of land. (2) Joint owners are -- (a) taken to be a single taxpayer; and
-- (b) jointly and severally liable for the full payment of the tax without regard to the relative shares or interests
-- in the land."
GIVEN `the land has more than one owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `each joint owner is liable for the full tax under s 14(2)(b)` IF `the land has more than one owner`

-- READING (finding 7): joint owners, being "a single taxpayer", are assessed on the land they own together, apart from
-- land any one of them owns alone.
`READING: land owned jointly is assessed apart from land a joint owner owns alone` MEANS TRUE

-- s 10(2): land tax "is due on a date the Commissioner determines or, if there is a sale, or transfer, of land by an
-- owner of land by whom land tax is payable, is due on the relevant day, within the meaning of section 39, in relation
-- to the sale or transfer, whichever date occurs first." s 39(10): "relevant day ... means -- (a) the day on which the
-- sale or transfer of land is completed; or (b)" a day the Commissioner sets by notice under s 39(9).
GIVEN `the date the Commissioner determines` IS A DATE, `the owner sells or transfers the land` IS A BOOLEAN, `the relevant day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day land tax is due under s 10(2)` MEANS
    IF `the owner sells or transfers the land` AND `is before` `the relevant day` `the date the Commissioner determines`
    THEN `the relevant day`
    ELSE `the date the Commissioner determines`

-- s 13(1): "If the amount of land tax payable in any financial year exceeds $500, the Commissioner may accept payment
-- of land tax for that financial year in a number of instalments determined by the Commissioner."
`the instalment threshold` MEANS 500

GIVEN `the land tax for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may accept instalments under s 13(1)` IF
    `the land tax for the year` GREATER THAN `the instalment threshold`

§§ `ss 37 and 37A -- rebates`

-- s 37(1): "An owner of land may apply to the Commissioner for a rebate of land tax in relation to a financial year if
-- -- (a) the owner was an owner at the start of the financial year; and (b) during that financial year a dwelling was
-- constructed on the land and occupied as principal residence -- (i) by an owner of at least a 50% interest in the land
-- or a related person of such an owner; or (ii) by a person who owns 50% or more of the shares in the company that owns
-- the land [not encoded]; and (c) the occupier ... did not, during that financial year, own -- (i) in Tasmania any
-- other land classified as principal residence land; or (ii) in another State or a Territory any land which ... is
-- treated ... as the principal residence of the owner." (3): "the Commissioner, if satisfied that a rebate is payable,
-- is to grant a rebate equal to the amount of land tax paid." (4): if assessed but unpaid, the Commissioner may waive
-- the requirement to pay. The section sets no time for applying (finding 13).
DECLARE `Building a home` HAS
    `the owner was an owner at the start of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `during the year a dwelling was built on the land and occupied as principal residence by an owner of at least 50% or a related person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `during the year the occupier owned other principal residence land in Tasmania, or a principal residence elsewhere in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Building a home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for a rebate under s 37` IF
        `the facts`'s `the owner was an owner at the start of the financial year`
    AND `the facts`'s `during the year a dwelling was built on the land and occupied as principal residence by an owner of at least 50% or a related person`
    AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `during the year the occupier owned other principal residence land in Tasmania, or a principal residence elsewhere in Australia`))

-- s 37A(1): "The owner of land may apply ... for a rebate of land tax paid if at the commencement of a financial year
-- the owner was -- (a) the owner of principal residence land; and (b) the owner of other land -- (i) that was purchased
-- with the intention that it become the principal residence land of the owner; or (ii) that was the principal
-- residence land of the owner in the period of 3 months preceding the commencement of the financial year." (2): "A
-- rebate is payable in respect of the land tax paid on the other land." (3): the Commissioner "is to grant" it if
-- satisfied that "(a) the owner became the owner of the principal residence land or the other land during the period of
-- 3 months preceding the commencement of the financial year; and (b) the principal residence land of the owner was --
-- (i) the principal residence land of the owner in the period of 3 months preceding the commencement of the financial
-- year; or (ii) the other land became the principal residence land of the owner in the financial year; and (c) before
-- 1 October of the financial year the owner entered into a contract to sell or otherwise disposed of -- (i) the
-- principal residence land; or (ii) the other land -- and the new owner took possession of the land in the financial
-- year; and (d) no rent or other income was derived from the principal residence land or the other land during the
-- period in which the owner owned both ...; and (e) the owner did not recover a proper proportion of any land tax paid
-- or payable in accordance with section 40(1); and (f) an application ... has been lodged ... (i) after the sale or
-- other disposition of the land and the new owner has taken possession ...; and (ii) not later than 3 months after the
-- end of the financial year." (4): "a person is an owner of land if the person is the owner of 50% or more of the
-- principal residence land and 50% or more of the other land." (f) is the regulative rule below.
DECLARE `Moving between two homes` HAS
    `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
    `at 1 July the owner owned 50% or more of principal residence land and 50% or more of other land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other land was bought to become the owner's principal residence land, or was it in the 3 months before 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the owner became owner of the principal residence land` IS A DATE
    `the day the owner became owner of the other land` IS A DATE
    `the principal residence land was the owner's principal residence land in the 3 months before 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other land became the owner's principal residence land during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the owner contracted to sell or otherwise disposed of one of the two` IS A DATE
    `the new owner took possession during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rent or other income was derived from either while the owner owned both` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner recovered a proportion of the land tax from the buyer under s 40(1)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "the period of 3 months preceding the commencement of the financial year": 1 April to 30 June before that 1 July.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls in the 3 months before the financial year` IF
        `is on or before` (YearMonthDay `the financial year` 4 1) `the day`
    AND `is before` `the day` (`1 July of` `the financial year`)

GIVEN `the move` IS A `Moving between two homes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conditions of s 37A(1) and (3)(a)-(e) are met` IF
        `the move`'s `at 1 July the owner owned 50% or more of principal residence land and 50% or more of other land`
    AND `the move`'s `the other land was bought to become the owner's principal residence land, or was it in the 3 months before 1 July`
    AND (    `falls in the 3 months before the financial year` (`the move`'s `the day the owner became owner of the principal residence land`) (`the move`'s `the financial year`)
         OR  `falls in the 3 months before the financial year` (`the move`'s `the day the owner became owner of the other land`) (`the move`'s `the financial year`))
    AND (    `the move`'s `the principal residence land was the owner's principal residence land in the 3 months before 1 July`
         OR  `the move`'s `the other land became the owner's principal residence land during the financial year`)
    AND `is before` (`the move`'s `the day the owner contracted to sell or otherwise disposed of one of the two`) (YearMonthDay (`the move`'s `the financial year`) 10 1)
    AND `the move`'s `the new owner took possession during the financial year`
    AND (NOT (`the move`'s `rent or other income was derived from either while the owner owned both`))
    AND (NOT (`the move`'s `the owner recovered a proportion of the land tax from the buyer under s 40(1)`))

-- s 37A(3)(f)(ii): "not later than 3 months after the end of the financial year" -- 30 September after it ends.
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for a s 37A rebate` MEANS YearMonthDay (`the financial year` PLUS 1) 9 30

§§ `s 11(5)-(6) -- a new owner's statement of interest`

-- s 11(5): "If it appears to the Commissioner that a person has become the owner of the land and the Commissioner has
-- not received any details or advice, the Commissioner, by notice served on the person, may require the person to
-- state any interest in the land." (6): "The statement is to be -- (a) by statutory declaration; and (b) lodged with
-- the Commissioner within 14 days after service of the notice." Serving the notice is the Commissioner's choice; once
-- served, the duty is the person's. Section 11 sets no penalty (the Taxation Administration Act 1997, not deposited,
-- may).
`the days to lodge the statement under s 11(6)` MEANS 14

GIVEN `a notice under s 11(5) has been served on the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must state their interest in the land under s 11(5)-(6)` IF
    `a notice under s 11(5) has been served on the person`

§§ `s 16 -- notice of a change in the use of land`

-- s 16: "An owner of land must, within 30 days, notify the Commissioner in writing, if -- (a) the land ceases to be
-- principal residence land, ceases to be primary production land, ceases to be exempt land or ceases to be land to
-- which section 30A applies; or (b) a factor that is relevant to determining whether or not, or the extent to which,
-- the land, or a part of the land, is principal residence land, primary production land or exempt land, has altered;
-- or (c) all or part of the land has ceased to be, or has become, land that the Commissioner is required to apportion
-- under section 19A, 19B or 19C or section 30A. Penalty: Fine not exceeding 10 penalty units."
`the days to notify under s 16` MEANS 30

`the most penalty units for an offence against s 16` MEANS 10

DECLARE `Change in use` HAS
    `the land ceased to be principal residence land, primary production land or exempt land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a factor relevant to whether, or how far, it is principal residence, primary production or exempt land altered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land ceased to be, or became, land to be apportioned under s 19A, 19B, 19C or 30A` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the change` IS A `Change in use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner must notify under s 16` IF
        `the change`'s `the land ceased to be principal residence land, primary production land or exempt land`
    OR  `the change`'s `a factor relevant to whether, or how far, it is principal residence, primary production or exempt land altered`
    OR  `the change`'s `the land ceased to be, or became, land to be apportioned under s 19A, 19B, 19C or 30A`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the owner and the Commissioner`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day the rule starts (stated with each rule).

-- s 10(2): the tax is due on its due day. Clock starts on the day of the assessment notice.
GIVEN `days from the notice to the due day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 10(2) -- the owner must pay the land tax by the day it is due` IS
    PARTY `the owner`
    MUST  `pay the land tax`
    WITHIN `days from the notice to the due day`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "s 10(2): land tax is due on the date the Commissioner determines, or on completion of a sale or transfer if earlier"

-- s 11(5)-(6): the statement by statutory declaration, lodged within 14 days after service. Clock starts on the day
-- the notice is served.
GIVEN `a notice under s 11(5) has been served on the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 11(5)-(6) -- the owner served with a notice must state their interest by statutory declaration within 14 days` IS
    IF `the person must state their interest in the land under s 11(5)-(6)` `a notice under s 11(5) has been served on the person`
    THEN PARTY `the owner`
         MUST  `lodge a statutory declaration stating the interest in the land`
         WITHIN `the days to lodge the statement under s 11(6)`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "s 11(5)-(6): a person served with the Commissioner's notice must state their interest in the land by statutory declaration lodged with the Commissioner within 14 days after service"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 13(1)-(2): where instalments are accepted, "If a taxpayer fails to pay an instalment by the due date for that
-- instalment, the Commissioner may require the taxpayer to pay the full amount of land tax for the financial year
-- within a specified period." Clock starts on the day the instalment is set.
GIVEN `days to the instalment's due date` IS A NUMBER, `the Commissioner requires the full amount` IS A BOOLEAN, `the specified period in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 13 -- the owner must pay each instalment, or may be required to pay the full year's tax` IS
    PARTY `the owner`
    MUST  `pay the instalment`
    WITHIN `days to the instalment's due date`
    LEST
        IF `the Commissioner requires the full amount`
        THEN PARTY `the owner`
             MUST  `pay the full amount of the land tax for the year`
             WITHIN `the specified period in days`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "s 13(2): after a missed instalment the full amount of land tax for the year must be paid within the period the Commissioner specifies"
        ELSE BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "s 13(2): an instalment was not paid by its due date"

-- s 16: within 30 days. Clock starts on the day of the change.
GIVEN `the change` IS A `Change in use`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 16 -- the owner must notify the Commissioner of a change within 30 days` IS
    IF `the owner must notify under s 16` `the change`
    THEN PARTY `the owner`
         MUST  `notify the Commissioner in writing of the change`
         WITHIN `the days to notify under s 16`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "s 16: an owner must notify the Commissioner in writing within 30 days; fine not exceeding 10 penalty units"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 37: the owner may apply (no time is set); on the application the Commissioner, if satisfied, "is to grant a rebate
-- equal to the amount of land tax paid". Applying is a choice. No period binds the Commissioner.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Building a home`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 37 -- the owner may apply, and the Commissioner is to grant a rebate equal to the land tax paid` IS
    IF `may apply for a rebate under s 37` `the facts`
    THEN PARTY `the owner`
         DO    `apply for the s 37 rebate`
         HENCE (PARTY `the Commissioner`
                MUST  `grant a rebate equal to the land tax paid`)
         LEST  FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 37A(3)(f): the application is lodged after the new owner took possession and "not later than 3 months after the
-- end of the financial year". Clock starts on the day the new owner took possession; the seat works out the days to
-- 30 September after the year. A late application, or none, loses the rebate but is no breach.
GIVEN `the move` IS A `Moving between two homes`, `days from possession to the last day to apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 37A -- the owner may apply by 30 September after the year, and the Commissioner is to grant the rebate` IS
    IF `the conditions of s 37A(1) and (3)(a)-(e) are met` `the move`
    THEN PARTY `the owner`
         DO    `apply for the s 37A rebate`
         WITHIN `days from possession to the last day to apply`
         HENCE (PARTY `the Commissioner`
                MUST  `grant a rebate of the land tax paid on the other land`)
         LEST  FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
